[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API","page":"API","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Modules","page":"API","text":"Order = [:module]","title":"Modules"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Types-and-constants","page":"API","text":"Order = [:type, :constant]","title":"Types and constants"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Functions-and-macros","page":"API","text":"Order = [:macro, :function]","title":"Functions and macros"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Documentation","page":"API","text":"","title":"Documentation"},{"category":"module","location":"api/#LegendDSP.LegendDSP","page":"API","text":"LegendDSP\n\nTemplate for Julia packages.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.LegendDSP"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendDSP.DSPConfig","page":"API","text":"DSPConfig{T <: Real}\n\nConfiguration parameters for DSP algorithms.\n\nFields\n\nenc_pickoff::Quantity{<:T}: pick-off time for ENC noise calculations\nbl_window::ClosedInterval{Quantity{<:T}}: fit window for basline extraction\ntail_window::ClosedInterval{Quantity{<:T}}: fit window for decay time extraction\ninTraceCut_std_threshold::T: in-trace pile-up rejector threshold in standard deviations\nt0_threshold::T: ADC threshold for t0 determination\ne_grid_rt_trap::StepRangeLen{Quantity{<:T}}: rise time grid scan range for trapezoidal filter\ne_grid_ft_trap::StepRangeLen{Quantity{<:T}}: flat-top time grid scan range for trapezoidal filter\ne_grid_rt_zac::StepRangeLen{Quantity{<:T}}: rise time grid scan range for ZAC filter\ne_grid_ft_zac::StepRangeLen{Quantity{<:T}}: flat-top time grid scan range for ZAC filter\ne_grid_rt_cusp::StepRangeLen{Quantity{<:T}}: rise time grid scan range for CUSP filter\ne_grid_ft_cusp::StepRangeLen{Quantity{<:T}}: flat-top time grid scan range for CUSP filter\na_grid_wl_sg::StepRangeLen{Quantity{<:T}}: window length grid scan range for SG filter\na_grid_wl_mwa::StepRangeLen{Quantity{<:T}}: window length grid scan range for MWA filter\na_mwa_windows::Vector{Quantity{<:T}}: fixed MWA window lengths stored as a_mwa_<ns> columns\na_mwa_passes::Int: number of alternating moving average passes of the MWA current filter\na_sg_windows::Vector{Quantity{<:T}}: fixed SG window lengths stored as a_sg_<ns> columns\nlq_windows::Vector{Vector{Quantity{<:T}}}: [early, gap, late] integration windows of the LQ parameters; one column lq80_<early><gap><late> (and lq90_…, lqamax_…) per window\n\nExamples\n\nusing LegendDSP\nusing LegendDataManagement\n\nl200 = LegendData(:l200)\nfilekey = start_filekey(l200, (:p03, :r000, :cal))\ndsp_config = DSPConfig(dataprod_config(l200).dsp(filekey).default)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.DSPConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendDSP.DerivativeFilter","page":"API","text":"struct DerivativeFilter <: AbstractRadIIRFilter\n\nWorking example:\n\nusing LegendDSP\nusing Unitful\n\nsignal = rand(100)\nt = range(0u\"ms\", 20u\"ms\", 100)\n\nwf = RDWaveform(t, signal)\nflt = DerivativeFilter()\nwf_new = flt(wf)\n\nConstructors:\n\nDerivativeFilter(; fields...)\n\nFields:\n\ngain::Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}: Filter gain\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.DerivativeFilter"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendDSP.IntersectMaximum","page":"API","text":"struct IntersectMaximum <: Function\n\nFinds the intersects of a Y with a threshold and picking the maximum in a given time window. Constructors:\n\nIntersectMaximum(; fields...)\n\nFields:\n\nmintot::Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}: minimum time-over-threshold\nmaxtot::Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}: maximum time-over-threshold for max to appear\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.IntersectMaximum"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendDSP.ModifiedSincFilter","page":"API","text":"struct ModifiedSincFilter{T<:RealQuantity} <: AbstractRadFIRFilter{}\n\nA Modified-Sinc filter Working example\n\nusing RadiationDetectorSignals\nusing Unitful\n\nn = 600\nnoise = 1.\nt = range(0u\"μs\", 20u\"μs\", 2*n)\nsignal = vcat(zeros(n), 10*ones(n)) + (noise*rand(2*n) .- noise/2)\nwf = RDWaveform(t, signal)\n\n# define filter parameters and filter\nflt = ModifiedSincFilter(d=4, m=1u\"μs\")\n\n# apply filter to signal\nwf_new = flt(wf)\n\nConstructors:\n\nModifiedSincFilter(; fields...)\n\nFields:\n\nd::Int64: degree of the filter determining the number of extrema in the kernel\nm::Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}: half-width of the kernel\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.ModifiedSincFilter"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendDSP.MovingWindowFilter","page":"API","text":"struct MovingWindowFilter <: AbstractRadFIRFilter\n\napply left moving average window to signal. The exact computations are:\n        yₙ = yₙ₋₁ + (xₙ - x₁)/l,    for n ∈ {1, …, l}\n        yₙ = yₙ₋₁ + (xₙ - xₙ₋ₗ)/l,    for n ∈ {l+1, …, L}\n\n\nConstructors:\n\nMovingWindowFilter(; fields...)\n\nFields:\n\nlength::Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}: length of the moving average window\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.MovingWindowFilter"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendDSP.MovingWindowMultiFilter","page":"API","text":"struct MovingWindowMultiFilter <: AbstractRadFIRFilter\n\napply passes moving average windows of size length to the signal, alternating forward and backward in time (left, right, left for the default three passes; an even number of passes is symmetric). Working example:\n\nusing RadiationDetectorSignals\nusing Unitful\n\nsignal = rand(100)\nt = range(0u\"ms\", 20u\"ms\", 100)\n\nwf = RDWaveform(t, signal)\nflt = MovingWindowMultiFilter(1u\"ms\")              # three passes left, right, left\nflt = MovingWindowMultiFilter(1u\"ms\"; passes = 2)  # left, right\nwf_new = flt(wf)\n\nConstructors:\n\nMovingWindowMultiFilter(; fields...)\nMovingWindowMultiFilter(length; passes = 3)\n\nFields:\n\nlength::Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}: size of the moving average window\npasses::Int64: number of moving average passes, alternating forward and backward in time\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.MovingWindowMultiFilter"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendDSP.MultiIntersect","page":"API","text":"struct MultiIntersect <: Function     Finds the x values at which a signal exceeds the provided      threshold_ratios the first time.      Constructors:     * MultiIntersect(; fields...)     Fields:\n\nthreshold_ratios::Vector{Float64}: ratios which determine the thresholds\nmintot::Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}: minimum time-over-threshold\nn::Int64: half window length of polynomial fit\nd::Int64: degree of polynomial\nsampling_rate::Int64: upsampling rate\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.MultiIntersect"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendDSP.TimeAxisFilter","page":"API","text":"struct TimeAxisFilter <: AbstractRadIIRFilter\n\nUpdates the time range step to period and shifts the time axis by offset.\n\nWorking example:\n\nusing LegendDSP\nusing RadiationDetectorSignals\nusing Unitful\n\nsignal = rand(100)\nt = range(0u\"ms\", 20u\"ms\", 100)\n\nwf = RDWaveform(t, signal)\nflt = TimeAxisFilter(4u\"ns\")\nwf_new = flt(wf)\n\nConstructors:\n\nTimeAxisFilter(; fields...)\n\nFields:\n\nperiod::Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}: Filter period\noffset::Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}: Filter offset\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.TimeAxisFilter"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendDSP.WeightedSavitzkyGolayFilter","page":"API","text":"struct WeightedSavitzkyGolayFilter{T<:RealQuantity} <: AbstractRadFIRFilter\n\nA Weighted-Savitzky-Golay filter. Working example:\n\nusing RadiationDetectorSignals\nusing Unitful\n\nn = 600\nnoise = 1.\nt = range(0u\"μs\", 20u\"μs\", 2*n)\nsignal = vcat(zeros(n), 10*ones(n)) + (noise*rand(2*n) .- noise/2)\nwf = RDWaveform(t, signal)\n\n# define filter parameters and filter\nflt = WeightedSavitzkyGolayFilter(length=1u\"μs\", degree=3, weightType=2)\n\n# apply filter to signal\nwf_new = flt(wf)\n\nConstructors:\n\nWeightedSavitzkyGolayFilter(; fields...)\n\nFields:\n\nlength::Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}: total filter length\ndegree::Int64: Polynomial degree\nweightType::Int64: weight function to use\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.WeightedSavitzkyGolayFilter"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendDSP.WhittakerHendersonFilter","page":"API","text":"struct WhittakerHendersonFilter <: AbstractRadSigFilter{LinearFiltering}\n\nA Whittaker-Henderson filter. Working example: ```julia using RadiationDetectorSignals using Unitful\n\nn = 600 noise = 1. t = range(0u\"μs\", 20u\"μs\", 2n) signal = vcat(zeros(n), 10ones(n)) + (noiserand(2n) .- noise/2) wf = RDWaveform(t, signal)\n\ndefine filter parameters and filter\n\nflt = WhittakerHendersonFilter(p=3, λ=4)\n\napply filter to signal\n\nwf_new = flt(wf)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.WhittakerHendersonFilter"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP._create_dsp_config-Tuple{PropDicts.PropDict}","page":"API","text":"_create_dsp_config(dsp_metadata::PropDicts.PropDict)\n\nCreate a DSPConfig from a PropDict of DSP metadata.\n\nArguments\n\ndsp_metadata::PropDicts.PropDict: DSP metadata\n\nReturns\n\ndsp_config::DSPConfig: DSP configuration\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP._create_dsp_config"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP._lq_column_name-Tuple{Symbol, Any}","page":"API","text":"_lq_column_name(t_start::Symbol, windows)\n\nColumn name of an LQ parameter: lq<start>_<early><gap><late> with the start timepoint without its leading t/t_ and the three window lengths in units of 0.1 µs with two digits, e.g. _lq_column_name(:t80, [2.5, 0.0, 2.5]u\"µs\") == :lq80_250025.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP._lq_column_name"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.align_waveform-Tuple{RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform, Any, Any}","page":"API","text":"align_waveform(wvf::RDWaveform, t_align, t_target)\n\nShift wvf in time so that the feature at t_align lands at t_target. The output has the time axis and length of the input; its value at time t is the input at t + (t_align - t_target), interpolated with a cubic Catmull-Rom spline through the four nearest samples. Positions outside the record repeat the first or last sample.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.align_waveform"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.align_waveforms-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, AbstractVector, Any}","page":"API","text":"align_waveforms(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, t_align::AbstractVector, t_target)\n\nalign_waveform for every waveform with its own alignment time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.align_waveforms"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.aligned_windows-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, Any, Integer, Integer}","page":"API","text":"aligned_windows(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, t_target, n_pre::Integer, n_post::Integer)\n\nSamples from n_pre before to n_post after the sample at t_target, one column per waveform. Throws if the window leaves the record, or if the waveforms do not share one time axis.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.aligned_windows"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.banded_cholesky_solve!-Tuple{AbstractVector, AbstractMatrix, AbstractVector}","page":"API","text":"banded_cholesky_solve!(x::AbstractVector, A::AbstractMatrix, y::AbstractVector)\n\nsolve the linear equation AA'x = y and store the result in x, where A is the cholesky decomposition of a banded centro symmetric matrix. A[1, i] is the diagonal, A[2, i] is the first subdiagonal and so on.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.banded_cholesky_solve!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.choleskyL!-Union{Tuple{AbstractMatrix{T}}, Tuple{T}} where T","page":"API","text":"choleskyL!(b::AbstractMatrix{T})\n\ninplace cholesky decomposition of a banded symmetric matrix, where  b[1, i] contains the diagonal elements, b[2, i] the elements of the  first subdiagonal and so on.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.choleskyL!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dplms_binned_reference-Tuple{AbstractMatrix, AbstractVector{<:Integer}, Real}","page":"API","text":"dplms_binned_reference(windows::AbstractMatrix, bins::AbstractVector{<:Integer}, plateau::Real)\n\nReference constraints per drift-time bin: the superpulse r_b of every bin b in bins, each divided by the common plateau, combined into mat = mean_b r_b r_bᵀ and vec = mean_b r_b. Bins are numbered 1:maximum(bins) and every bin must hold an event. Returns (mat, vec, refs) with refs the per-bin references stacked into one column per bin.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dplms_binned_reference"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dplms_default_grid-Tuple{Integer}","page":"API","text":"dplms_default_grid(n_rise::Integer; nm = 1.0, za = 1e3, ft = 1.0, ct = 0.0, ff_factors = 1:4)\n\nDPLMS grid of flat-top widenings ff = k·n_rise samples for k in ff_factors, all at the weights nm, za, ft, ct in units of the reference amplitude. Only weight ratios matter, and in these units any za above about 1 already enforces zero area; za = 0 switches the zero-area condition off.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dplms_default_grid"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dplms_flattop_matrix-Tuple{AbstractMatrix, Integer}","page":"API","text":"dplms_flattop_matrix(windows_wide::AbstractMatrix, ff::Integer)\n\nFlat-top matrix for a filter of n = size(windows_wide, 1) - 2ff samples, from aligned pulse shapes (one column each, e.g. events or superpulses) widened by ff samples on each side. It is the mean over columns and over the 2ff shifts of the outer product of the column's first difference, so xᵀ F x is the mean squared slope of the filter output around the pick-off.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dplms_flattop_matrix"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dplms_noise_matrix-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, IntervalSets.ClosedInterval, Integer}","page":"API","text":"dplms_noise_matrix(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, bl_window::ClosedInterval, n::Integer)\n\nNoise matrix for a filter of n samples: the mean of b bᵀ over every window b of n consecutive samples inside bl_window of every waveform. The waveforms must be baseline subtracted; a residual offset appears as a rank-one term, not as noise. When the baseline mean subtracted from the waveforms was estimated over the same window, the lowest-frequency noise power is underestimated by about n divided by the number of baseline samples.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dplms_noise_matrix"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dplms_reference-Tuple{AbstractMatrix, AbstractUnitRange{<:Integer}}","page":"API","text":"dplms_reference(windows::AbstractMatrix, plateau::AbstractUnitRange)\n\nSuperpulse of the aligned windows (one column per event): the row mean divided by its mean over the plateau rows, so the reference has unit amplitude after the rise. Returns (ref, plateau) with the divisor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dplms_reference"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dplms_synthesis-Tuple{AbstractMatrix, AbstractVector, AbstractMatrix, Any}","page":"API","text":"dplms_synthesis(noise, ref, flattop, binned; nm, za, ft, ct = 0)\n\nSolve the DPLMS system\n\n(nm·noise + ref refᵀ + za·𝟙 + ft·flattop + ct·binned.mat) x = ref + ct·binned.vec\n\nfor the filter coefficients x along the window and rescale them so that x ⋅ ref == 1. 𝟙 is the all-ones matrix, so za penalizes the squared coefficient sum. Returns\n\ncoeffs: the impulse response, reverse(x), for ConvolutionFilter(DirectConvolution(), coeffs); the filter output at the last sample of a window equals x ⋅ window,\nnoise_out: sqrt(xᵀ noise x), the predicted output noise in units of the reference amplitude,\nzero_area: sum(x).\n\nnm, za, ft and ct act only through their ratios: scaling all four by the same factor gives the same filter after normalization.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dplms_synthesis"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_aux-Union{Tuple{Q}, Tuple{Q, DSPConfig}} where Q<:TypedTables.Table","page":"API","text":"dsp_aux(data::Q, config::DSPConfig) where {Q <: Table}\n\nDSP for auxiliary channels whose waveforms are spikes. For each waveform, the baseline-subtracted maximum sample and its time are returned as e_max and t_max.\n\nThe config argument is accepted for consistency with the other detector DSP entry points but is not used.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_aux"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_aux_compressed-Union{Tuple{Q}, Tuple{Q, DSPConfig}} where Q<:TypedTables.Table","page":"API","text":"dsp_aux_compressed(data::Q, config::DSPConfig) where {Q <: Table}\n\nCompressed-data variant of dsp_aux. The presummed waveforms are decoded before their maxima and maximum times are determined. Each baseline is scaled by the corresponding presumming rate before it is subtracted.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_aux_compressed"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_cusp_ft_optimization-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{T}, Unitful.Quantity{T}}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"dsp_cusp_ft_optimization(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity{T}, rt::Quantity{T}) where T<:Real\n\nGet energy grid values for given CUSP grid rise times while varying the flat-top time.\n\nReturns\n\n- `e_grid`: Array energy values for the given CUSP rise time grid at a given flat-top time grid.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_cusp_ft_optimization"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_cusp_rt_optimization-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{T}}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"dsp_cusp_rt_optimization(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity{T},; ft::Quantity{T}=4.0u\"µs\") where T<:Real\n\nGet ENC noise grid values for given CUSP grid rise times.\n\nReturns\n\n- `enc_cusp_grid`: Array ENC noise values for the given CUSP rise time grid\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_cusp_rt_optimization"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_decay_times-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, IntervalSets.ClosedInterval{<:Union{Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s101\", 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s101\", 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {var\"#s101\"<:T, U}}, IntervalSets.ClosedInterval{<:Union{Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s99\", 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s99\", 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {var\"#s99\"<:T, U}}}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"dsp_decay_times(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, bl_window::ClosedInterval{<:Unitful.Time{<:T}}, tail_window::ClosedInterval{<:Unitful.Time{<:T}})\ndsp_decay_times(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig)\n\nGet statistics on the logarhithmic of the tail of the wvfs in the interval tail_window.\n\nReturns\n\nτ: decay time in µs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_decay_times"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_dplms_energy-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, AbstractVector, AbstractVector, Any, IntervalSets.ClosedInterval, RadiationDetectorDSP.SignalEstimator}","page":"API","text":"dsp_dplms_energy(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, coeffs::AbstractVector, t50::AbstractVector, t_pickoff, current_window::ClosedInterval, signal_estimator::SignalEstimator)\n\nApply the DPLMS filter coeffs to baseline-subtracted, pole-zero-corrected waveforms and read the energy at t50 + t_pickoff with signal_estimator. Returns (e, emax) with emax the maximum of the filter output inside current_window shifted by t_pickoff, where the read-out times of all events with t50 inside current_window lie.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_dplms_energy"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_dplms_optimization-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{<:Real}, AbstractVector}","page":"API","text":"dsp_dplms_optimization(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity, drift::AbstractVector;\n    n_pre = nothing, n_post = nothing, n_noise_windows = 8, ff_level = 0.999, n_bins = 5, plateau_length = 20, flat_tol = 1e-3, grid = dplms_default_grid)\n\nSynthesize DPLMS energy filters on presummed waveforms for every point of grid and return the energies they give. A grid point is a NamedTuple with the weights nm, za, ft, ct and the flat-top widening ff in samples.\n\nSteps: baseline subtraction over config.bl_window; pole-zero correction with InvCRFilter(τ); t50, the time where half of the current integral is reached: 50 % of the 10/10 µs trapezoid maximum, found with get_threshold (config.kwargs_pars.tx_mintot) as t50_pre in dsp_icpc_compressed; alignment of every waveform to the sample nearest the median t50; windows of n_pre samples before to n_post after that sample; noise matrix from the baseline window; reference and one reference per drift-time bin, the bins being n_bins quantiles of drift; flat-top matrix from the drift-bin references widened by ff samples. All matrices are in units of the reference amplitude, the mean over the last plateau_length window samples.\n\nUnless given, n_pre and n_post equal (n_bl - n_noise_windows) ÷ 2 with n_bl the number of samples inside config.bl_window: the longest symmetric window that leaves n_noise_windows sliding windows per event for the noise matrix. A window as long as the baseline leaves the constant mode of the noise matrix undetermined, because the baseline mean is subtracted over the same region, so only zero-area filters (za > 0) are meaningful for long windows.\n\nEvery grid point yields a filter applied to the unaligned pole-zero-corrected waveforms with the energy read at t50 + t_pickoff, t_pickoff = n_post·Δt. The flat-top term penalizes the output slope of every drift-bin reference shifted by up to ff samples, so the output stays flat while any of these shapes moves by ff samples. n_rise is the number of samples after the alignment point until the slowest drift-bin reference reaches ff_level of the plateau. grid is either a vector of grid points or a function of n_rise returning one, e.g. grid = n -> dplms_default_grid(n; za = 0) for filters without the zero-area condition.\n\nflat_top and shaping_time describe each filter's output for the full-length drift-bin references. The flat top is the interval around the read-out time where every filtered reference stays within flat_tol of its value at the read-out time; the shaping time runs from the first sample where the filtered superpulse exceeds flat_tol to the start of the flat top.\n\nReturns\n\ne_grid, emax_grid: energies and filter-output maxima, size (length(grid), length(wvfs))\ncoeffs: impulse response per grid point; t_pickoff\nnoise_out, zero_area: predicted relative output noise and coefficient sum per grid point\nflat_top, shaping_time: one time per grid point\ngrid, ref, ref_bins (one column per bin), t50 (per event), plateau, n_pre, n_post, n_rise\nsuperpulse: the aligned superpulse in units of the reference amplitude\nsuperpulse_bins: the aligned superpulse of every drift-time bin, same units\nresponse: superpulse filtered with coeffs, one RDWaveform per grid point\nnoise, flattops: the noise matrix and the flat-top matrix per ff (a Dict), in units of the reference amplitude\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_dplms_optimization"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_icpc-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Q}, Tuple{Q, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{T}, PropDicts.PropDict}} where {Q<:TypedTables.Table, T<:Real}","page":"API","text":"dsp_icpc(data::Q, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity{T}, pars_filter::PropDict) where {Q <: Table, T<:Real}\n\nDSP for ICPC detectors. It needs the decay time τ of the detector and the filter parameters pars_filter for the optimal filter parameters for the Trap, CUSP and ZAC filter. \n\nInput data\n\nThe input data is a table with the following columns:\n\nwaveform: waveform data\nbaseline: baseline from FADC\ntimestamp: timestamp from FADC\neventnumber: event ID from FADC\ndaqenergy: energy from FADC\n\nOutput data\n\nThe output data is a table with the following columns:\n\nblmean: baseline mean\nblsigma: baseline sigma\nblslope: baseline slope\nbloffset: baseline offset\ntailmean: tail mean after PZ correction\ntailsigma: tail sigma after PZ correction\ntailslope: tail slope after PZ correction\ntailoffset: tail offset after PZ correction\nt0: start time of waveform drift\nt10: timepoint of 10% of the pulse amplitude (maximum of the 101010 trapezoid)\nt50: timepoint of 50% of the pulse amplitude (maximum of the 101010 trapezoid)\nt80: timepoint of 80% of the pulse amplitude (maximum of the 101010 trapezoid)\nt90: timepoint of 90% of the pulse amplitude (maximum of the 101010 trapezoid)\nt99: timepoint of 99% of the pulse amplitude (maximum of the 101010 trapezoid)\nt50_current: timepoint of current rise to 50% of maximum\nt_amax: quadratically interpolated timepoint of maximum current\ntail_τ: tail decay time\ntail_mean: tail mean before PZ correction\ntail_sigma: tail sigma before PZ correction\ne_max: maximum of waveform\ne_min: minimum of waveform\ne_10410: energy of waveform with trapezoidal filter of 10µs rise time with 4µs flat-top\ne_313: energy of waveform with trapezoidal filter of 3µs rise time with 1µs flat-top\ne_101010: energy of waveform with trapezoidal filter of 10µs rise time with 10µs flat-top\na_sg: maximum of the current from the Savitzky-Golay derivative (sg_flt_degree) with the optimized window length from the aoeopt pars\na_sg_<ns>: the same with the fixed window lengths a_sg_windows of the config\na_raw: maximum of the raw current (simple derivative)\na_mwa: maximum of the raw current after the multi-pass moving-window average (a_mwa_passes, alternating left and right) with the optimized window length from the aoeopt pars\na_mwa_<ns>: the same with the fixed window lengths a_mwa_windows of the config\nt_a_sg, t_a_mwa: quadratically interpolated timepoints of the a_sg and a_mwa maxima\ne_10410_inv: maximum of inverted waveform with trapezoidal filter of 10µs rise time with 4µs flat-top\ne_313_inv: maximum of inverted waveform with trapezoidal filter of 3µs rise time with 1µs flat-top\nt0_inv: start time of inverted waveform drift\ne_trap: energy of waveform with trapezoidal filter of optimized rise and flat-top time\ne_cusp: energy of waveform with CUSP filter of optimized rise and flat-top time\ne_zac: energy of waveform with ZAC filter of optimized rise and flat-top time\nqdrift: Q-drift parameter\nlq80_<early><gap><late>, lq90_…, lqamax_…: LQ parameters from t80, t90 and t_amax, charge in the late window minus charge in the early window, one column per [early, gap, late] of lq_windows in the config (lengths in 0.1 µs, e.g. lq80_250025: 2.5 µs early, no gap, 2.5 µs late)\nblfc: baseline from FADC\ntimestamp: timestamp from FADC\neventID_fadc: event ID from FADC\ne_fc: energy from FADC\npretrace_diff: difference between first sample and baseline mean\ndrift_time: drift time between t0 and 90% of waveform maximum\ninTrace_intersect: position of in-trace pile-up\ninTrace_n: multiplicity of in-trace pile-up\nn_sat_low: number of samples the waveform is saturated at low of FADC range\nn_sat_high: number of samples the waveform is saturated at high of FADC range\nn_sat_low_cons: number of consecutive samples the waveform is saturated at low of FADC range\nn_sat_high_cons: number of consecutive samples the waveform is saturated at high of FADC range\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_icpc"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_icpc_compressed-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Q}, Tuple{Q, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{T}, PropDicts.PropDict}} where {Q<:TypedTables.Table, T<:Real}","page":"API","text":"dsp_icpc_compressed(data::Q, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity{T}, pars_filter::PropDict) where {Q <: Table, T<:Real}\n\nDSP for ICPC detectors. It needs the decay time τ of the detector and the filter parameters pars_filter for the optimal filter parameters for the Trap, CUSP and ZAC filter. \n\nInput data\n\nThe input data is a table with the following columns:\n\nwaveform: waveform data\nbaseline: baseline from FADC\ntimestamp: timestamp from FADC\neventnumber: event ID from FADC\ndaqenergy: energy from FADC\n\nOutput data\n\nThe output data is a table with the following columns:\n\nblmean: baseline mean\nblsigma: baseline sigma\nblslope: baseline slope\nbloffset: baseline offset\ntailmean: tail mean after PZ correction\ntailsigma: tail sigma after PZ correction\ntailslope: tail slope after PZ correction\ntailoffset: tail offset after PZ correction\nt0: start time of waveform drift\nt10: timepoint of 10% of the pulse amplitude (maximum of the 101010 trapezoid)\nt50: timepoint of 50% of the pulse amplitude (maximum of the 101010 trapezoid)\nt80: timepoint of 80% of the pulse amplitude (maximum of the 101010 trapezoid)\nt90: timepoint of 90% of the pulse amplitude (maximum of the 101010 trapezoid)\nt99: timepoint of 99% of the pulse amplitude (maximum of the 101010 trapezoid)\nt50_current: timepoint of current rise to 50% of maximum\nt_amax: quadratically interpolated timepoint of maximum current\ntail_τ: tail decay time\ntail_mean: tail mean before PZ correction\ntail_sigma: tail sigma before PZ correction\ne_max: maximum of waveform\ne_min: minimum of waveform\ne_10410: energy of waveform with trapezoidal filter of 10µs rise time with 4µs flat-top\ne_313: energy of waveform with trapezoidal filter of 3µs rise time with 1µs flat-top\ne_101010: energy of waveform with trapezoidal filter of 10µs rise time with 10µs flat-top\na_sg: maximum of the current from the Savitzky-Golay derivative (sg_flt_degree) with the optimized window length from the aoeopt pars\na_sg_<ns>: the same with the fixed window lengths a_sg_windows of the config\na_raw: maximum of the raw current (simple derivative)\na_mwa: maximum of the raw current after the multi-pass moving-window average (a_mwa_passes, alternating left and right) with the optimized window length from the aoeopt pars\na_mwa_<ns>: the same with the fixed window lengths a_mwa_windows of the config\nt_a_sg, t_a_mwa: quadratically interpolated timepoints of the a_sg and a_mwa maxima\ne_10410_inv: maximum of inverted waveform with trapezoidal filter of 10µs rise time with 4µs flat-top\ne_313_inv: maximum of inverted waveform with trapezoidal filter of 3µs rise time with 1µs flat-top\nt0_inv: start time of inverted waveform drift\ne_trap: energy of waveform with trapezoidal filter of optimized rise and flat-top time\ne_cusp: energy of waveform with CUSP filter of optimized rise and flat-top time\ne_zac: energy of waveform with ZAC filter of optimized rise and flat-top time\ne_dplms: energy of waveform with the optimized DPLMS filter (pars_filter.dplms), or the trapezoidal filter of flt_defaults.dplms if there is none, read out at t50_pre + t_pickoff\ne_dplms_max: maximum of the DPLMS filter output inside the current window shifted by t_pickoff\nqdrift: Q-drift parameter\nlq80_<early><gap><late>, lq90_…, lqamax_…: LQ parameters from t80, t90 and t_amax, charge in the late window minus charge in the early window, one column per [early, gap, late] of lq_windows in the config (lengths in 0.1 µs, e.g. lq80_250025: 2.5 µs early, no gap, 2.5 µs late)\nblfc: baseline from FADC\ntimestamp: timestamp from FADC\neventID_fadc: event ID from FADC\ne_fc: energy from FADC\npretrace_diff: difference between first sample and baseline mean\ndrift_time: drift time between t0 and 90% of waveform maximum\ninTrace_intersect: position of in-trace pile-up\ninTrace_n: multiplicity of in-trace pile-up\nn_sat_low: number of samples the waveform is saturated at low of FADC range\nn_sat_high: number of samples the waveform is saturated at high of FADC range\nn_sat_low_cons: number of consecutive samples the waveform is saturated at low of FADC range\nn_sat_high_cons: number of consecutive samples the waveform is saturated at high of FADC range\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_icpc_compressed"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_mwa_optimization-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{T}, PropDicts.PropDict}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"dsp_mwa_optimization(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity{T}, pars_filter::PropDict; f_evaluate_qc::Union{Function, Missing}=missing) where T<:Real\n\nOptimize the window length of the MWA current filter (MovingWindowMultiFilter on the simple-derivative current) for the A/E parameter, same scheme as dsp_sg_optimization.\n\nArguments\n\n- `f_evaluate_qc`: Optional ML QC evaluation function. If missing, default qc_label=-1 is used.\n\nReturns\n\n- `aoe`: A/E values for each MWA window length in `config.a_grid_wl_mwa`\n- `energy`: Array of energy values\n- `blmean`: Baseline mean value\n- `blslope`: Baseline slope value\n- `t50`: 50% rise time of the waveform\n- `qc_label`: QC labels (-1 if no ML model available)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_mwa_optimization"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_mwa_optimization_compressed-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{T}, PropDicts.PropDict}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"dsp_mwa_optimization_compressed(wvfs_wdw::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, wvfs_pre::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity{T}, pars_filter::PropDict; presum_rate::Real=T(8), f_evaluate_qc::Union{Function, Missing}=missing)\n\nOptimize the window length of the MWA current filter (MovingWindowMultiFilter on the simple-derivative current) for the A/E parameter, same scheme as dsp_sg_optimization_compressed.\n\nReturns\n\n- `aoe`: A/E values for each MWA window length in `config.a_grid_wl_mwa`\n- `energy`: Array of energy values\n- `blmean`: Baseline mean value\n- `blslope`: Baseline slope value\n- `t50`: 50% rise time of the presummed waveform\n- `qc_label`: QC labels (-1 if no ML model available)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_mwa_optimization_compressed"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_puls-Union{Tuple{Q}, Tuple{Q, DSPConfig}} where Q<:TypedTables.Table","page":"API","text":"dsp_puls(data::Q, config::DSPConfig) where {Q <: Table}\n\nDSP function for pulser processing.\n\nInput data\n\nThe input data is a table with the following columns:\n\nwaveform: waveform data\nbaseline: baseline data\ntimestamp: timestamp data\neventnumber: event number data\ndaqenergy: energy data\n\nOutput data\n\nThe output data is a table with the following columns:\n\nblmean: baseline mean\nblsigma: baseline sigma\nblslope: baseline slope\nbloffset: baseline offset\nt50: timepoint of 50% of waveform maximum\ne_max: maximum of waveform\ne_10410: energy of waveform with trapezoidal filter of 10µs rise time with 4µs flat-top\nblfc: baseline from FADC\ntimestamp: timestamp\neventID_fadc: event number from FADC\ne_fc: energy from FADC\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_puls"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_puls_compressed-Union{Tuple{Q}, Tuple{Q, DSPConfig}} where Q<:TypedTables.Table","page":"API","text":"dsp_puls_compressed(data::Q, config::DSPConfig) where {Q <: Table}\n\nDSP function for pulser processing.\n\nInput data\n\nThe input data is a table with the following columns:\n\nwaveform: waveform data\nbaseline: baseline data\ntimestamp: timestamp data\neventnumber: event number data\ndaqenergy: energy data\n\nOutput data\n\nThe output data is a table with the following columns:\n\nblmean: baseline mean\nblsigma: baseline sigma\nblslope: baseline slope\nbloffset: baseline offset\nt50: timepoint of 50% of waveform maximum\ne_max: maximum of waveform\ne_10410: energy of waveform with trapezoidal filter of 10µs rise time with 4µs flat-top\nblfc: baseline from FADC\ntimestamp: timestamp\neventID_fadc: event number from FADC\ne_fc: energy from FADC\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_puls_compressed"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_qc_flt_optimization-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Union{Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s106\", 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s106\", 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {var\"#s106\"<:Real, U}, Function}","page":"API","text":"dsp_qc_flt_optimization(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Unitful.Time{<:Real}, f_evaluate_qc::Union{Function, Missing})\n\nGet QC DSP for filter parameter optimization for a given waveform set. If fevaluateqc is missing, skips expensive ML classification and sets qclabel=-1. Columns as for [`dspqcfltoptimization_compressed`](@ref).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_qc_flt_optimization"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_qc_flt_optimization_compressed-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Union{Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s106\", 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s106\", 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {var\"#s106\"<:Real, U}, Function}","page":"API","text":"dsp_qc_flt_optimization_compressed(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Unitful.Time{<:Real}, f_evaluate_qc::Union{Function, Missing})\n\nGet QC DSP for filter parameter optimization for a given waveform set. If fevaluateqc is missing, skips expensive ML classification and sets qc_label=-1.\n\nColumns: energy (default trapezoid), blmean, blsigma, blslope, t50 (half of the waveform maximum), t50_pre (half of the 10 µs rise, 10 µs flat-top trapezoid maximum, the t50 of dsp_dplms_optimization) and qc_label.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_qc_flt_optimization_compressed"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_qdrift_flt_optimization-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, Vector{<:Real}, DSPConfig, Union{Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s103\", 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s103\", 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {var\"#s103\"<:Real, U}}","page":"API","text":"dsp_qdrift_flt_optimization(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, blmean::Vector{<:Real}, config::DSPConfig, τ::Unitful.Time{<:Real})\n\nGet QDrift filter parameter optimization for a given waveform set.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_qdrift_flt_optimization"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_sg_optimization-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{T}, PropDicts.PropDict}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"dsp_sg_optimization(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity{T}, pars_filter::PropDict; f_evaluate_qc::Union{Function, Missing}=missing) where T<:Real\n\nOptimize the Savitzky-Golay filter parameters for a given waveform set.\n\nArguments\n\n- `f_evaluate_qc`: Optional ML QC evaluation function. If missing, default qc_label=-1 is used.\n\nReturns\n\n- `aoe`: Array of efficiency values for the given Savitzky-Golay filter parameters\n- `energy`: Array of energy values for the given Savitzky-Golay filter parameters\n- `blmean`: Baseline mean value\n- `blslope`: Baseline slope value\n- `qc_label`: QC labels (-1 if no ML model available)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_sg_optimization"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_sg_optimization_compressed-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{T}, PropDicts.PropDict}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"dsp_sg_optimization_compressed(wvfs_wdw::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, wvfs_pre::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity{T}, pars_filter::PropDict; presum_rate::Real=T(8), f_evaluate_qc::Union{Function, Missing}=missing) where T<:Real\n\nOptimize the Savitzky-Golay filter parameters for a given waveform set.\n\nArguments\n\n- `f_evaluate_qc`: Optional ML QC evaluation function. If missing, default qc_label=-1 is used.\n\nReturns\n\n- `aoe`: Array of efficiency values for the given Savitzky-Golay filter parameters\n- `energy`: Array of energy values for the given Savitzky-Golay filter parameters\n- `blmean`: Baseline mean value\n- `blslope`: Baseline slope value\n- `qc_label`: QC labels (-1 if no ML model available)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_sg_optimization_compressed"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_sg_sipm_optimization_compressed","page":"API","text":"dsp_sg_sipm_optimization_compressed(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, dsp_config::PropDict, optimization_config::PropDict)\n\nThis function calculates DSP grid to find the optimal thresholds for the SiPMs.\n\nArguments\n\nwvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms: Array of RDWaveforms\ndsp_config::PropDict: Configuration parameters for the DSP\noptimization_config::PropDict: Configuration parameters for the optimization\n\nReturns\n\nTable: Table with the optimal thresholds for the SiPMs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_sg_sipm_optimization_compressed"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_sg_sipm_thresholds_compressed-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, Union{Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s106\", 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s106\", 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {var\"#s106\"<:Real, U}, PropDicts.PropDict}","page":"API","text":"dsp_sg_sipm_thresholds_compressed(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::PropDict)\n\nThis function calculates the baseline of the waveforms and the baseline of the waveforms with the sign flipped. The function is used to calculate the thresholds for the SiPMs.\n\nArguments\n\nwvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms: Array of RDWaveforms\nconfig::PropDict: Configuration parameters\n\nReturns\n\nTable: Table with the baseline of the waveforms and the baseline of the waveforms with the sign flipped\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_sg_sipm_thresholds_compressed"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_sipm-Union{Tuple{Q}, Tuple{Q, PropDicts.PropDict, PropDicts.PropDict}} where Q<:TypedTables.Table","page":"API","text":"dsp_sipm(data::Q, config::PropDict, pars_threshold::PropDict)\n\nDSP routine for SiPM data. It needs the threshold parameters from the threshold scan for the given SiPM channel as well as the discharge threshold parameters.\n\nInput data\n\nThe input data is a table with the following columns:\n\nwaveform: waveform data\nbaseline: baseline data\ntimestamp: timestamp data\neventnumber: event number data\ndaqenergy: energy data\n\nOutput data\n\nThe output data is a table with the following columns:\n\nblfc: baseline from FADC\ntimestamp: timestamp\neventID_fadc: event number from FADC\ne_fc: energy from FADC\nt_max, t_min: time of waveform maximum/minimum\nt_max_lar, t_min_lar: time of waveform maximum/minimum in LAr window\ne_max, e_min: waveform maximum/minimum amplitude\ne_max_lar, e_min_lar: waveform maximum/minimum amplitude in LAr window\nblmean, blsigma, blslope, bloffset: baseline statistics\nwfmean, wfsigma, wfslope, wfoffset: waveform statistics\n\nSG filter columns\n\nthreshold_sg: SG trigger threshold\nthreshold_DC_sg: SG discharge trigger threshold\ntrig_pos_sg: SG trigger positions\ntrig_max_sg: SG trigger maxima\ntrig_pos_DC_sg: SG discharge trigger positions\ntrig_max_DC_sg: SG discharge trigger maxima\n\nTrap filter columns\n\nthreshold_trap: trap trigger threshold\nthreshold_DC_trap: trap discharge trigger threshold\ntrig_pos_trap: trap trigger positions\ntrig_pos_high_trap: trap trigger high positions\ntrig_pos_tot_trap: trap trigger time-over-threshold positions\ntrig_max_trap: trap trigger maxima\ntrig_pos_DC_trap: trap discharge trigger positions\ntrig_pos_high_DC_trap: trap discharge trigger high positions\ntrig_pos_tot_DC_trap: trap discharge trigger time-over-threshold positions\ntrig_max_DC_trap: trap discharge trigger maxima\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_sipm"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_sipm_compressed-Union{Tuple{Q}, Tuple{Q, PropDicts.PropDict, PropDicts.PropDict}} where Q<:TypedTables.Table","page":"API","text":"dsp_sipm_compressed(data::Q, config::PropDict, pars_threshold::PropDict)\n\nDSP routine for SiPM data. It needs the threshold parameters from the threshold scan for the given SiPM channel as well as the discharge threshold parameters.\n\nInput data\n\nThe input data is a table with the following columns:\n\nwaveform: waveform data\nbaseline: baseline data\ntimestamp: timestamp data\neventnumber: event number data\ndaqenergy: energy data\n\nOutput data\n\nThe output data is a table with the following columns:\n\nblfc: baseline from FADC\ntimestamp: timestamp\neventID_fadc: event number from FADC\ne_fc: energy from FADC\nt_max, t_min: time of waveform maximum/minimum\nt_max_lar, t_min_lar: time of waveform maximum/minimum in LAr window\ne_max, e_min: waveform maximum/minimum amplitude\ne_max_lar, e_min_lar: waveform maximum/minimum amplitude in LAr window\nblmean, blsigma, blslope, bloffset: baseline statistics\nwfmean, wfsigma, wfslope, wfoffset: waveform statistics\n\nSG filter columns\n\nthreshold_sg: SG trigger threshold\nthreshold_DC_sg: SG discharge trigger threshold\ntrig_pos_sg: SG trigger positions\ntrig_max_sg: SG trigger maxima\ntrig_pos_DC_sg: SG discharge trigger positions\ntrig_max_DC_sg: SG discharge trigger maxima\n\nTrap filter columns\n\nthreshold_trap: trap trigger threshold\nthreshold_DC_trap: trap discharge trigger threshold\ntrig_pos_trap: trap trigger positions\ntrig_pos_high_trap: trap trigger high positions\ntrig_pos_tot_trap: trap trigger time-over-threshold positions\ntrig_max_trap: trap trigger maxima\ntrig_pos_DC_trap: trap discharge trigger positions\ntrig_pos_high_DC_trap: trap discharge trigger high positions\ntrig_pos_tot_DC_trap: trap discharge trigger time-over-threshold positions\ntrig_max_DC_trap: trap discharge trigger maxima\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_sipm_compressed"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_trap_ft_optimization-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{T}, Unitful.Quantity{T}}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"dsp_trap_ft_optimization(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity{T}, rt::Quantity{T}) where T<:Real\n\nGet energy grid values for given trap grid rise times while varying the flat-top time.\n\nReturns\n\n- `e_grid`: Array energy values for the given trap rise time grid at a given flat-top time grid.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_trap_ft_optimization"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_trap_rt_optimization-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{T}}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"dsp_trap_rt_optimization(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity{T},; ft::Quantity{T}=4.0u\"µs\") where T<:Real\n\nGet ENC noise grid values for given trap grid rise times.\n\nReturns\n\n- `enc_trap_grid`: Array ENC noise values for the given trap rise time grid\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_trap_rt_optimization"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_zac_ft_optimization-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{T}, Unitful.Quantity{T}}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"dsp_zac_ft_optimization(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity{T}, rt::Quantity{T}) where T<:Real\n\nGet energy grid values for given ZAC grid rise times while varying the flat-top time.\n\nReturns:     - e_grid: Array energy values for the given ZAC rise time grid at a given flat-top time grid.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_zac_ft_optimization"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.dsp_zac_rt_optimization-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, DSPConfig, Unitful.Quantity{T}}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"dsp_zac_rt_optimization(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, config::DSPConfig, τ::Quantity{T},; ft::Quantity{T}=4.0u\"µs\") where T<:Real\n\nGet ENC noise grid values for given ZAC grid rise times.\n\nReturns\n\n- `enc_zac_grid`: Array ENC noise values for the given ZAC rise time grid\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.dsp_zac_rt_optimization"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.extrema3points-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{T, T, T}} where T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}","page":"API","text":"extrema3points(y1::T,y2::T,y3::T)::T where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nCalculate the extrema of a parabola defined by three points.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.extrema3points"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#LegendDSP.extremestats","page":"API","text":"extremestats(signal::AbstractSamples, start::Real, stop::Real)\nextremestats(signal::RDWaveform, start::RealQuantity, stop::RealQuantity)\n\nGet the extrema and their time positions on signal in the interval (start,stop). Output is in the format (min = .., max = .., tmin = .., tmax = ..)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.extremestats"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.get_a-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, IntervalSets.ClosedInterval{<:Union{Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s103\", 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s103\", 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {var\"#s103\"<:Real, U}}}","page":"API","text":"get_a(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, current_window::ClosedInterval{<:Unitful.Time{<:Real}})\n\nMaximum of the current waveforms wvfs in current_window, quadratically interpolated around the maximum sample (get_wvf_maximum). Returns the maxima max and their timepoints t.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.get_a"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.get_dplms_pars-Tuple{PropDicts.PropDict, DSPConfig, Union{Unitful.Quantity{T, 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{T, 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {T, U}}","page":"API","text":"get_dplms_pars(pd::PropDict, config::DSPConfig, Δt::Unitful.Time)\n\nDPLMS filter for dsp_dplms_energy as (; coefficients, t_pickoff), with t_pickoff the read-out time after t50. Returns pd.dplms if present. Otherwise builds the trapezoidal filter of config.default_flt_param.dplms (rt, ft) sampled at Δt, read out at rt + ft/2; it gives the same energies as TrapezoidalChargeFilter(rt, ft).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.get_dplms_pars"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.get_lq-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, Array{<:Union{Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s97\", 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s97\", 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {var\"#s97\"<:Real, U}}, Union{Unitful.Quantity{T, 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{T, 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {T, U}, Union{Unitful.Quantity{T, 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{T, 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {T, U}, Union{Unitful.Quantity{T, 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{T, 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {T, U}}","page":"API","text":"get_lq(wvfs_int::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, t_start::Array{<:Unitful.Time}, early::Unitful.Time, gap::Unitful.Time, late::Unitful.Time; pol_power::Int=3, sign_est_length::Unitful.Time=100u\"ns\")\n\nLQ parameter: charge in the late window [t_start + early + gap, t_start + early + gap + late] minus the charge in the early window [t_start, t_start + early]. wvfs_int are the integrated waveforms (IntegratorFilter(1).(wvfs)), so the integration is done once for all LQ variants. get_qdrift(wvfs, t, Δt) equals get_lq(wvfs_int, t, first(Δt), 0, last(Δt) - first(Δt)).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.get_lq"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#LegendDSP.get_qc_classifier","page":"API","text":"get_qc_classifier(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, f_evaluate_qc::Function)\n\nGet a classifier for quality cuts using the given waveforms and evaluation function which evulates a predefined SVM model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.get_qc_classifier"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#LegendDSP.get_qc_classifier_compressed","page":"API","text":"get_qc_classifier_compressed(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, f_evaluate_qc::Function)\nget_qc_classifier_compressed(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, f_evaluate_qc::Function, config::DSPConfig)\n\nGet a classifier for quality cuts using the given waveforms and evaluation function which evulates a predefined SVM model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.get_qc_classifier_compressed"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.get_qc_ml_func-Tuple{Matrix{<:Real}, Vector{<:Real}, PropDicts.PropDict}","page":"API","text":"get_qc_ml_func(dwts_norm::Matrix{<:Real}, dc_labels::Vector{<:Real}, hyperparams::PropDict)\n\nCreate a function that takes a signal and returns the prediction using the given hyperparameters and discrete wavelet transforms.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.get_qc_ml_func"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.get_qdrift-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, Array{<:Union{Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s91\", 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s91\", 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {var\"#s91\"<:Real, U}}, StepRangeLen{<:Union{Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s89\", 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s89\", 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {var\"#s89\"<:Real, U}}}","page":"API","text":"get_qdrift(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, t_start::Array{Unitful.Time{T}}, Δt::UnitRange{Unitful.Time{T}}; pol_power::Int=3, sign_est_length::Unitful.Time=100u\"ns\")\n\nGet the Q-drift parameter for each waveform in wvfs by integrating the waveform with gain = 1 and using a polynomial signal estimator of order pol_power and length sign_est_length to estimate the signal.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.get_qdrift"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.get_t0-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, T}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"get_t0(wvfs_pz::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, t0_threshold::T) where T<:Real\n\nGet t0 for each waveform in wvfs_pz by using a fast asymetric trapezoidal filter and a fixed threshold at t0_threshold. The filter is truncated to the range 0µs to 60µs where the Ge trigger is expected in FlashCam.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.get_t0"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.get_threshold-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, Union{Array{T}, T}}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"get_threshold(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, threshold::Array{T}) where T<:Real\n\nGet threshold for each waveform in wvfs by intersecting the waveform with a threshold per waveform or globally.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.get_threshold"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.get_triggers-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, Real, IntervalSets.ClosedInterval{<:Union{Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s97\", 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s97\", 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {var\"#s97\"<:Real, U}}}","page":"API","text":"get_triggers(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, sigma_threshold::Real, bl_window::ClosedInterval{<:Unitful.Time{<:Real}}; mintot::Unitful.Time=100.0u\"ns\")\n\nDetermine trigger positions and multiplicities from waveforms.\n\nThe triggers are identified as intersections of the signal with a threshold defined as a multiple of the baseline standard deviation within bl_window.\n\nReturns a named tuple containing the trigger positions (intersect) and the corresponding trigger multiplicities (n).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.get_triggers"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.get_triggers_reversed-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}, Real, IntervalSets.ClosedInterval{<:Union{Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s97\", 𝐓, U}, Unitful.Level{L, S, Unitful.Quantity{var\"#s97\", 𝐓, U}} where {L, S}} where {var\"#s97\"<:Real, U}}}","page":"API","text":"get_triggers_reversed((wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms, sigma_threshold::Real, bl_window::ClosedInterval{<:Unitful.Time{<:Real}}; mintot::Unitful.Time=100.0u\"ns\")\n\nDetermine trigger positions and multiplicities from waveforms.\n\nThe triggers are identified as intersections of the reversed signal with a threshold defined as a multiple of the baseline standard deviation within bl_window.\n\nReturns a named tuple containing the trigger positions (intersect) and the corresponding trigger multiplicities (n).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.get_triggers_reversed"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#LegendDSP.get_wvf_maximum","page":"API","text":"get_wvf_maximum(signal::AbstractSamples, start::Real, stop::Real)\nget_wvf_maximum(signal::RDWaveform, start::RealQuantity, stop::RealQuantity)\n\nGet the maximum of a signal and its time in the interval (start, stop) by quadratic interpolation.\n\nReturns (max = ..., t = ...).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.get_wvf_maximum"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.makeFitWeights-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{U, Int64}} where U<:Integer","page":"API","text":"makeFitWeights(d::Int, m::Int) where {U}\n\nreturn the weights for the linear fit user for linear extrapolation at  at the right boundary.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.makeFitWeights"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.makeIPlusLambdaDprimeD-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{T, Int64, Int64}} where T","page":"API","text":"makeIPlusLambdaDprimeD(λ::T, p::Int, N::Int) where {T}\n\nbuild the centro symmetric banded matrix which needs to be inverted  later: I + λ*D'D D is the finite difference matrix of order p.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.makeIPlusLambdaDprimeD"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#LegendDSP.saturation","page":"API","text":"tailstats(signal::AbstractSamples, start::Real, stop::Real)\ntailstats(signal::RDWaveform, start::RealQuantity, stop::RealQuantity)\n\nGet statistics on the logarhithmic of the tail of a signal in the interval (start,stop).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.saturation"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#LegendDSP.tailstats","page":"API","text":"tailstats(signal::AbstractSamples, start::Real, stop::Real)\ntailstats(signal::RDWaveform, start::RealQuantity, stop::RealQuantity)\n\nGet statistics on the logarhithmic of the tail of a signal in the interval (start,stop) by fitting a linear function.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.tailstats"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#LegendDSP.thresholdstats","page":"API","text":"thresholdstats(signal::AbstractSamples, min::Real, min::Real)\nthresholdstats(signal::RDWaveform, min::RealQuantity, max::RealQuantity)\n\nGet the standard deviation of all samples in a signal that are within  the lower bound min and the upper bound max. If no values for min or max are passed, the respective bound is ignored.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.thresholdstats"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#LegendDSP.thresholdstats_mad","page":"API","text":"thresholdstats_mad(signal::AbstractSamples, min::Real, max::Real)\nthresholdstats_mad(signal::RDWaveform, min::RealQuantity, max::RealQuantity)\n\nGet a robust threshold estimate using the Median Absolute Deviation (MAD) of all samples in a signal that are within the lower bound min and the upper bound max. The MAD is scaled by 1.4826 to be consistent with the standard deviation for normally distributed data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.thresholdstats_mad"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendDSP.weighted_linear_reg-Tuple{AbstractVector, AbstractVector}","page":"API","text":"weighted_linear_reg(w::AbstractVector, y::AbstractVector)\n\nDo a weighted linear regression of the data y with weights w and return the offset and slope. its assumed that x is a range from 1 to length(y)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendDSP.weighted_linear_reg"},{"category":"section","location":"LICENSE/#LICENSE","page":"LICENSE","text":"MIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2018 Oliver Schulz <oschulz@mpp.mpg.de>, Florian Henkes <florian.henkes@tum.de>, Felix Hagemann <hagemann@mpp.mpg.de>, and contributors\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.\n\n","title":"LICENSE"},{"category":"section","location":"#LegendDSP.jl","page":"Home","text":"","title":"LegendDSP.jl"}]
